# A creature another effect makes a nonbasic land loses its rules text to Blood Moon too (CR 305.7), and every rule read
# off its card goes with it (KI-52: whether a land loses its rules text is judged on it as layer 4 leaves it, not as layers 1
# to 3 made it). Omni-Changeling, entering under Life and Limb alone, keeps its copy ability (it would be a Forest land there,
# but nothing takes its abilities) and copies Bot2's Thalia, Guardian of Thraben "except it has changeling" (CR 707.9b): a
# Saproling, so Life and Limb makes it a 1/1 Forest land too. Under both Thalias Blood Moon costs {2}{R} plus {2}
# ("Noncreature spells cost {1} more to cast"). Once Blood Moon is on the battlefield, Bot1's Omni-Thalia is a nonbasic land
# Blood Moon makes a Mountain - Blood Moon applies to it only after Life and Limb made it a land (CR 613.8a) - and it loses
# its rules text, its tax among it; Bot2's Thalia, no Saproling and no land, keeps hers. So Bot1's Lotus Petal ({0}) costs
# {1}: Mox Pearl alone pays it. (Bot2's Thalia is the only creature to copy, so the copy's choice
# takes it by default: a name with a comma cannot be written in a choice.)

